{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/DLSSUpscaling","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/adaengine\/dlssupscaling"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AdaEngine"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"DLSS Upscaling"},"abstract":[{"text":"Render a 3D view below its output resolution and reconstruct it with NVIDIA DLSS Super Resolution, or denoise a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"path-traced view with DLSS Ray Reconstruction. DLSS is optional: without it a camera uses the portable temporal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reconstruction that ships with the engine, and nothing else changes.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Requirements","anchor":"Requirements"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An NVIDIA GeForce RTX GPU with a current driver, running the Vulkan renderer (Windows today)."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The NVIDIA DLSS SDK. Its license is NVIDIA’s, so AdaEngine never contains or downloads it. Clone","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"https:\/\/github.com\/NVIDIA\/DLSS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" yourself and accept its terms before using it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Set up the runtime","anchor":"Set-up-the-runtime"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Build the small AdaEngine bridge once against your copy of the SDK. It writes ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"adaengine_ngx.dll"},{"text":" and copies the NGX","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"libraries next to it:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["python ada_tool.py build ngx-bridge --sdk path\/to\/DLSS --output path\/to\/ngx"],"syntax":"bash"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Point the engine at that folder with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ADAENGINE_NGX_SDK_PATH"},{"type":"text","text":" environment variable, or put the files next to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"game executable. Both the bridge and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nvngx_dlss.dll"},{"type":"text","text":" must be in the same folder; ship "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nvngx_dlssd.dll"},{"type":"text","text":" too if you use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Ray Reconstruction. Only absolute folders are searched, never the current directory or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PATH"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Use it on a camera","type":"heading","anchor":"Use-it-on-a-camera"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Choose DLSS on the camera’s temporal upscaling settings. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"renderScale"},{"type":"text","text":" is the ratio of internal to output resolution,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the engine picks the closest DLSS preset:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["camera.temporalUpscaling = .init(renderScale: 0.5, method: .dlss)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Render scale"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Preset","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DLAA"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"about 0.67","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Quality"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"about 0.58","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Balanced"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"0.5"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Performance"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"about 0.33"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ultra Performance","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":".automatic","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the default) uses DLSS when it is available and the portable reconstruction otherwise. "},{"code":".dlss","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" asks for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"DLSS and falls back to "},{"code":".portable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when it cannot run. "},{"code":".portable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" never uses DLSS; choose it to keep the portable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reconstruction on an RTX machine where the bridge is installed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Check-what-ran","text":"Check what ran","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DLSS initializes on the first frames after startup. Until it is ready, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".dlss"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".automatic"},{"type":"text","text":" cameras use the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"portable reconstruction."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Read the "},{"code":"TemporalReconstructionStatuses","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" resource from the render world (the world that runs the render systems) to see, per camera, the method that was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requested, the method in effect, the DLSS preset and, when DLSS was not used, the reason:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["if let status = statuses[cameraID], let reason = status.fallbackReason {","    print(\"DLSS not used: \\(reason)\")","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Ray-Reconstruction","level":2,"text":"Ray Reconstruction"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A path-traced view whose camera uses DLSS and traces at the DLSS input size is denoised and upscaled in one step by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Ray Reconstruction. Leave "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pathTracing.denoiser"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".automatic"},{"type":"text","text":", or set "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".rayReconstruction"},{"type":"text","text":" to request it. When it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cannot run, the view uses the portable denoiser and the path tracing statistics report why in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"denoiserFallback"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Limits","level":2,"text":"Limits"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"DLSS runs only through the Vulkan renderer on Windows; Linux, Metal and the web player use the portable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reconstruction.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Frame generation and the other DLSS features are not supported.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A DLSS failure at run time turns DLSS off for every camera for the rest of the session and the portable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reconstruction takes over. The frame that failed keeps whatever its output held.","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Building","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Contributing","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AdaUIIdentity","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/ImageDecoders","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AnimationAuthoring","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/CharacterLocomotion3D","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AnimationIK","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Atmosphere","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/GameDiagnosticsOverlay","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/MovieMaker","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/PipelinedRendering","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/HardwarePathTracing","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Terrain","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/ProceduralNoise","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/VisionOSWindowed"],"generated":true,"title":"Guides"}],"references":{"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/Atmosphere":{"url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/atmosphere","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give a 3D camera a physically based sky. The atmosphere scatters the sun’s light"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the way air does, so the sky turns from blue at noon to orange near the horizon","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and dark at night, the sun appears as a disc that the air reddens, and distant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"geometry fades into haze."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Atmosphere","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Atmosphere"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/GameDiagnosticsOverlay":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"See the game’s update rate while you play. The overlay shows "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"FPS"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Frame time"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in the top-left corner of the game window. Mouse and keyboard"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"input still reach the game under the overlay.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/GameDiagnosticsOverlay","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Game diagnostics overlay","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/gamediagnosticsoverlay"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/PipelinedRendering":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/PipelinedRendering","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/pipelinedrendering","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Render a scene one frame behind its simulation to overlap rendering with the next frame’s work."}],"type":"topic","title":"Pipelined Rendering"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/CharacterLocomotion3D":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/CharacterLocomotion3D","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/characterlocomotion3d","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CharacterLocomotion3DComponent"},{"type":"text","text":" to play skeletal animations from an upright 3D character’s"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"actual movement. Add it to the root entity that owns the character controller and skinned model."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Your input or AI continues to set "},{"code":"desiredVelocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"jumpRequested"},{"type":"text","text":". Locomotion reads the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"resolved motion after physics, so holding forward against a wall can leave the character idle.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Animate a 3D character from movement"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/AnimationAuthoring":{"url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/animationauthoring","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Copy an imported animation or capture a rest\/current pose into a project-owned"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animlib"},{"type":"text","text":" resource. Source GLB\/glTF bytes remain unchanged. Swift code, Studio’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Animator, the editor agent and project Tools share the same data and edit commands.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Authoring skeletal animation","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AnimationAuthoring"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/AnimationIK":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Constrain a skeletal chain after its clip, Animation Graph and visual LOD pose have been mixed."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/animationik","type":"topic","title":"Animation IK and pose modifiers","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AnimationIK"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/Building":{"abstract":[{"text":"This guide covers two scenarios:","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Building","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Building Ada","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/building"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/MovieMaker":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/MovieMaker","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a fresh game world at a fixed simulation rate, waiting for every GPU"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frame and disk write before advancing. Rendering speed never drops movie frames."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Configure the same gameplay plugins and cameras as your game in "},{"code":"make","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Platform\/window plugins are unnecessary for this offscreen runtime."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"MovieMaker","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MovieMaker"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/moviemaker","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MovieMaker"}]},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/AdaUIIdentity":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AdaUIIdentity","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/adauiidentity","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"AdaUI reconciles a new view tree against the mounted "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ViewNode"},{"text":" tree. A node is preserved only when the new node and old node describe the same identity and the new node can update the old node. Preserved nodes keep their ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", focus state, in-flight animation controllers, layers, and other node-local runtime state. Recreated nodes start with fresh runtime state."}],"type":"topic","title":"AdaUI View Identity"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/Contributing":{"abstract":[{"text":"We welcome contributions of all kinds: bug fixes, features, documentation, and examples.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Contributing","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Contributing to Ada","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/contributing"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/ProceduralNoise":{"abstract":[{"text":"Use a noise generator as a deterministic scalar field for terrain heights,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"procedural placement, or volume density. Import "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Math"},{"type":"text","text":" directly, or use its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"re-export from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdaEngine"},{"type":"text","text":". No GPU or editor state is needed."}],"url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/proceduralnoise","role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Procedural Noise","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/ProceduralNoise"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/VisionOSWindowed":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/VisionOSWindowed","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/visionoswindowed","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"visionOS Windowed Mode","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run Ada apps in visionOS Shared Space using the existing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WindowGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" scene model."}]},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine":{"abstract":[{"text":"Bringing simple and powerful game engine for your awesome games.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine","kind":"symbol","title":"AdaEngine"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/HardwarePathTracing":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Let a path-traced view find ray intersections with the GPU’s ray-tracing hardware instead of a shader BVH. The image,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lighting and denoisers stay the same; only the intersection step changes, and the shader BVH remains the fallback"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wherever hardware cannot be used.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/hardwarepathtracing","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Hardware Path Tracing","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/HardwarePathTracing"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/ImageDecoders":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/ImageDecoders","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/imagedecoders","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Load PNG, JPEG (","type":"text"},{"code":"jpg","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"jpeg","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), BMP and TGA images as CPU pixels using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Image","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or load a GPU texture through ","type":"text"},{"code":"Texture2D","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Loading images and adding formats"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/Terrain":{"url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/terrain","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create editable ground with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Terrain3D"},{"type":"text","text":". Its heights describe one square surface"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the entity’s local X\/Z plane. "},{"code":"Model3DPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" generates the visible geometry;","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Physics3DPlugin"},{"text":" adds matching static triangle collision.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Terrain","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Terrain"}}}